// expect-ok
// Z3 corpus #49: axis-1 — Wall 4 Step 6 pattern-match narrowing (positive).
//
// WHAT THIS FIXTURE PROVES
//
// Wall 4 Step 6 commit #3 introduces refinement narrowing through
// pattern matches: when a `match` arm destructures a refined variant,
// each pattern-bound identifier carries the variant's matching
// Literal-RHS refinement clauses on its `TypedExpr.refinement`
// sidecar (the same field Step 2 attaches to field-access reads).
//
// In this fixture, `match v { Positive(x) => ... }` binds `x` to the
// `Positive` variant's i64 payload. Per N9-S6 the i-th binding maps
// to the i-th declared field; per N22-S6 the attached clauses are
// filtered to `RefinementRhs::Literal` only. The binding's refinement
// is therefore `[x > 0]`.
//
// Inside the arm body, the construction `Positive(x)` re-builds a
// `SignedInt::Positive`. The construction-site dispatcher (Step 6
// commit #2's `check_variant_refinements_at_construction`) finds
// `x` is non-literal, but its preserved refinement subsumes the
// destination's `x > 0` predicate via Step 3's syntactic / Z3-backed
// implication path. The construction is accepted.
//
// WITHOUT narrowing (commit #2 alone), this fixture would fire T211
// because the supplied value is symbolic without preserved refinement.
//
// THE LANGUAGE PRIMITIVES THIS NEEDED
//
//   * Step 6 commit #2 named-payload + per-variant `where` clause.
//   * Step 6 commit #3 `pattern_refinement_stack` on MonomorphTracker.
//   * Step 6 commit #3 `lookup_pattern_refinement` in `infer_path_expr`.
//   * Step 2 `TypedExpr.refinement` sidecar (PR #61).
//   * Step 3 Z3-backed syntactic / semantic match dispatch (PR #62).
//
// MUTATION CONTRACT
//
// Replacing `Positive(x)` with `Positive(_)` (wildcard binding —
// fixture 51) drops the refinement; the downstream construction
// then fires T211.
module sigil;

enum SignedInt {
    Positive(x: i64) where x > 0,
    Negative(x: i64) where x < 0,
}

entry actor Main {
    on Tick() -> i64 {
        let v: SignedInt = Positive(7);
        match v {
            Positive(x) => { let p: SignedInt = Positive(x); return 1; },
            Negative(y) => { return 0 - 1; },
        }
    }
}
